# .dockerignore for beam4pm (rename this file to `.dockerignore` at the repo
# root when integrating). The Dockerfile COPYs only rebar.config, mix.exs,
# mix.lock, src/ and generated/, but docker still uploads the whole build
# context first -- without this file that context includes the full
# vendor/ggen-marketplace submodule and local build dirs (~500MB measured on
# the real scratch build of 2026-08-29 even with vendor excluded from the
# copy). Keeping the context lean also stops vendor/_build churn from
# invalidating the build-push-action type=gha layer cache.
.git/
.github/
vendor/
_build/
deps/
docs/
playground/
generated/gleam/build/

# Real bug caught 2026-08-31: a locally pre-built rust4pm-wasm engine (from
# running scripts/rust4pm_wasm_build.sh on the host before `docker build`,
# exactly what any contributor following CLAUDE.md's own build instructions
# would have done) leaks into the image via `COPY native ./native`, making
# BeamPM.Rust4PM.wasm_built?/0 return true DURING the Dockerfile's early
# `mix test` step -- which runs deliberately BEFORE its own
# `RUN bash scripts/rust4pm_wasm_build.sh` step, per that step's own
# comment. That flips test/beam4pm_rust4pm_test.exs's setup_all into its
# real-engine branch, which then raises on the canonical
# ~/wasm4pm/data/InternationalDeclarations.xes fixture path -- genuinely
# absent inside the container -- invalidating all 13 of that file's tests
# (`13 invalid`, not a clean skip). CI never hit this: GitHub Actions
# runners start from a clean checkout with no pre-built native/*/target/.
# Excluding every native oracle/engine crate's Rust build output keeps the
# image's own two-stage wasm-build ordering authoritative regardless of
# what the host machine has already compiled.
native/*/target/
